WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.980
Let’s say it’s the early 15th century
and you’re a young citizen of a northern

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.260
German city of Rostock, playing the new online
game Raid Shadow Legends.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:13.099
You begin this 3D online RPG by choosing a
starter hero to fight your battles with and

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:17.630
down the line can get many more heroes from
the summoning portal to build up a full team.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.970
With this rag tag group you can then complete
quests, challenges and progress through the

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:22.970
campaign.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.060
The graphics and animations of this game are
great looking, smoothless, the art style has

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.880
this delightful feeling of a sort of cartoonish
reality and you can get this charmingly looking

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.800
game right now on IOS, Android and PC with
cross platform support.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.680
That means you can play with your friends
no matter what potato they’re playing on.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.710
So what are you waiting for, as part of the
New Player Program there’s a special link

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.879
in the description that will give you 50k
silver to start off with, and a free epic

00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:52.809
champion to put in to that rag tag team you
plan to conquer the world with.

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:57.710
Good luck and thank you for Raid Shadow Legends
for sponsoring this video.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.960
Rostock is a very rich autonomous Hanseatic
city within the duchy of Mecklenburg and is

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.500
a valuable ship building port for the Hansa.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.090
Outside of Rostock, the hanseatic league has
many members.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:11.780
With its headquarters in Lubeck it operates
a very wide trade network across numerous

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.570
northern European cities.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.860
Some cities are members of the league just
like Rostock, others just have permanent representatives

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.720
of the league living in their city ensuring
a streamlined flow of trade goods.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.430
And some cities which are very important to
the Hanseatic league but aren’t autonomous

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:29.630
and are under the domain of a foreign monarch,
meaning the cities can’t join the league

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.250
fully, have what the Hansa calls a Kontor.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.381
Which is an independent part of a city, with
extra privileges granted by the local ruler

00:01:36.381 --> 00:01:39.490
that allows them to live under their own German
rules.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.240
Local rulers were usually strong-armed by
the League to give these extra privileges

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:48.360
to the Kontors, because Hansa was a very powerful
and rich entity in medieval northern Europe,

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.530
that rarely took no for an answer.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.630
Plus they brought a lot of trade to an area
which was always a plus for any local monarch.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:59.320
However going back to Rostock recently the
dukes of Mecklenburg have been trying to curb

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.150
the cities autonomy and bring it more into
the fold of their influence.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:07.020
Which is a very similar situation that many
other Hanseatic cities have found themselves

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.020
under recently.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.690
None the less you don’t care for grand politics
that seem to move very slowly, taking decades

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.250
to resolve sometimes.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.940
Plus the Hanseatic League seems to be at the
height of its power, it’s not like from

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.940
now on it’s going to gradually shrink due
to the exertion of more direct control by

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:26.440
local rulers and being pushed out by national
globalized trade companies that do business

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.780
across multiple continents, some of which
you don’t even know exist yet.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.390
That’s not gonna happen.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:35.550
You’re living here and now in Rostock, looking
to make money looking for a job.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:39.550
And there’s no better paying employer in
the city, than the Hanseatic League, a medieval

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:44.370
european trading guild of which your city
is a proud member of and from which the Hanseatic

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.090
league recruits young boys from.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.160
Ehhh Young boys?

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.560
Ou yes I forgot to mention you’re most likely
12, but that’s fine, it’s the middle ages,

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.110
so this is nothing unusual.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.340
With the offer of a home, a stable income,
an education, and a possibility to see the

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.780
world, you don’t hesitate to sign up.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:04.230
Now usually young boys are recruited by the
Hansa because one of their family members,

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.900
mostly their dad, is already a merchant in
the League.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.000
However this is not always the case so for
the sake of argument let's say your parents

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.930
died of a plague and one of your very close
family friends was a Hanseatic merchant who

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.400
helped you get signed up.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.970
Now Hansa didn’t only recruit 12 year olds,
you could have technically signed up at any

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:25.470
point in your life but the older you where
the less likely you where to get in.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.020
With that said, many young adults, usually
through family connections or their own influence,

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.720
often easily got into the League.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.020
But I digress.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.970
Before the Hansa accepts you, you have to
fulfill certain criteria.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:36.970
Are you male, check.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.780
Do you speak Low German, check.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.409
Are you Low German, check.

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:43.209
Have you lived in Rostock for more than 7
years, check.

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:48.760
Are you willing to remain unmarried/unattached
for a certain amount of time usually 7 to

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.920
10 years?

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.959
You might think this is a ridiculous question
since you’re twelve, but you’re actually

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:57.010
legally allowed to marry since 12 in most
of Medieval Europe.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:01.540
Even though this was rarely practiced by females
who usually married between 14 and 20, and

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:05.100
almost never practiced by males who usually
got married in their early twenties.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:10.599
But it did happen, so … sure what ta hell
check.

00:04:10.599 --> 00:04:15.080
Are you young, healthy, strong, basically
well suited for harsh manual labor, check.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.590
Can you be trusted with leagues trade secrets,
well if your YouTube comments are anything

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.990
to go by than no, but I’ll give it to you
anyways, check.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:27.400
These aren’t the only criteria and there
where many more criterias which changed depending

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.150
on what city you’re being recruited from,
what period of the Hanseatic league you’re

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:36.090
being recruited in, or just the literal preferences
of the person who’s doing the particular

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.150
recruitment.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:41.390
Nonetheless you pass all these criteria and
are awarded the title of Stubenjunge, office

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:46.389
boy or office helper and the league decides
you’ll be sent to live for 7 to 10 years

00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:49.210
in one of its most northern Kontors in Bergen.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:53.650
You promptly leave Rostock on one of the leagues
merchant ships, wondering if you’ll ever

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:59.990
see the city again, but are nonetheless excited
for what lies ahead.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:03.820
The reasons why the Hanseatic League even
operated in Bergen are multiple.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.229
The largest reason being the cod trade.

00:05:06.229 --> 00:05:09.920
Cod which is so numerous in the North See
unlike the herring of the Baltic sea which

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:15.000
Hansa relied upon before expanding its trade
northward is a much less oily fish, meaning

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.230
after being wind dried unlike the herring
it can last for years before going rotten.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.650
And the longer you can keep your trade good
liquid, the better.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:28.160
Plus on top of being a fairly large city with
plenty of access to the local North Sea fisheries

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:33.270
willing to sell their product, Bergen at this
time also had a sizeable German population.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.540
These Germans were mostly artizens like, cobblers,
tailors, etc. that came to Bergen due to the

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.160
lack of well made homegrown Norwagen goods.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:45.750
These two aspects and multiple otherones meant
that Bergen was the perfect city in Norway

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.520
for the Hansa to set up shop, and so they
did.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:52.990
You arrive in Bergen and the ship drops you
off on the north side of the harbor, the first

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:58.699
thing you see are large colorful wooden buildings,
surrounded by palisades, guarded by dogs and

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:01.110
seemingly separate from the rest of the city.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.690
What you see, is the Bergen Kontor, known
as Bryggen.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:09.230
The isolated nature of the Bryggen from the
rest of Bergen is on purpose.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:13.370
The Hanseatic League wants you to focus on
your work and nothing but the work, everything

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.600
else is a distraction.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:19.640
And even though this is the official standing
of the League it is rarely fully enforced.

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:24.331
The Bergen citizens often participate in Bryggens
social celebrations, the Bryggen merchants

00:06:24.331 --> 00:06:29.340
often have close Bergen friends, and the Kontor
even operates a public wine cellar for the

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.340
locals.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.229
Nonetheless you’re showed that each colorful
house is called a Yard which is where members

00:06:33.229 --> 00:06:37.410
of the league live, conduct business, have
social gatherings, etc.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:41.430
Each Yard is also divided depending on the
geographical area where the merchants come

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:42.430
from.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:46.910
So all merchants from Westphalia live in one
Yard while all merchants from Lower Saxony

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.910
live in another Yard, etc.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:52.610
Naturally since you’re from Rostock, you
are put in to the Yard where all merchants

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:55.039
from Mecklenburg and Pomerania live.

00:06:55.039 --> 00:06:58.760
Every Yard has a council comprised of all
the senior merchants living in it, the council

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:03.000
elects a house Master in charge of basically
everything that happens in the Yard.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.960
The Kontor as a whole also has three elected
elderman responsible for the entire Kontor

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:12.150
and the communication with the League itself,
and lastly the elderman are advised by an

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.790
elected council of 18 deputies.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:20.509
Each Yard also has its own flag and some amazing
name like, The Unicorn, The Golden Shoe or

00:07:20.509 --> 00:07:22.890
my personal favorite, The Sisters.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:27.300
So you're a newcomer to the Kontor and the
first night at the Sisters Yard you are promptly

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.800
hazed, which includes but isn’t limited
to, just simply getting punched and kicked,

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:36.610
being pelted by pieces of crap, getting ice
cold water poured on you and or being thrown

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:38.229
into the local well.

00:07:38.229 --> 00:07:42.199
After surviving that, you’re officially
part of the The Sisters Yard and of the Bergen

00:07:42.199 --> 00:07:46.550
Kontor and you can start working your way
up the Hanseatic Corporate ladder.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:51.099
Your official work as Stubenjunge involves
cleaning the Yard, the bathrooms, the ships,

00:07:51.099 --> 00:07:53.520
and also attending classes in the dining hall.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.919
Here you’re taught how to read and write
in german and sometimes latin, do basic math

00:07:57.919 --> 00:08:02.150
bookkeepings, and various merchant laws and
dues and don’t of the industry.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:06.490
You live in one room with 5 to 7 other young
members of the Kontor and are not allowed

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.870
to talk to the senior members of the League
unless spoken to.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:13.889
None the less you do your work, your studies
and get involved in the very close knit social

00:08:13.889 --> 00:08:17.300
community of the Kontor.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:21.420
Three years have passed and you have been
upgraded to a Bootsjunge, also there’s no

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:22.629
better way of putting it.

00:08:22.629 --> 00:08:23.940
You’re a teenager now.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:28.400
As a bootsjunge you no longer have to clean
the Kontor or the ships but are in charge

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.519
of taking care of the boats, which includes
everything from maintaining the boats, to

00:08:32.519 --> 00:08:36.479
making sure the boats are ready whenever needed,
and when they’re not needed making sure

00:08:36.479 --> 00:08:38.890
they are stored offshore so they wont be stolen.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.490
You’re further now required to be part of
the rowing crew of the boats as well.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:47.220
Plus, when the fishing season ends and Norwagens
from all around Norway come to Bergen to sell

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:51.589
their seasons catch, you’re awakened at
4 am and are put to work to whole all the

00:08:51.589 --> 00:08:53.440
new fish bought by the Hansa.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:09:02.320
You do this until 9 pm with only 2 short breaks
for breakfast and lunch.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.310
Also now that you’re 15 or maybe even when
you were younger, it’s very hard to gauge

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:10.320
the average age of sexual activity in the
middle ages, you start to participate in an

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.959
act that many other guys from the Kontor participate
in as well.

00:09:13.959 --> 00:09:17.920
And that is to sneak out at night to the street
that lies just north of Bryggen.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.730
This is because the street north of Bryggen
is known as the Bergens red light district.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:26.670
And since the Kontor is filled with young
males, all of whom vowed not to get married

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:31.520
or romantically attached for their 7 to 10
year stay at the Hansa Kontor, as one historian

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:36.260
puts it, “there was a large overdose of
testosterone that needed an outlet to prevent

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.770
violent clashes”.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:41.839
The league officially throwned upon these
practices, because as they put it, you “might

00:09:41.839 --> 00:09:46.310
tell the native woman under the influence
of her charm, as well as that of liquor, things

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.850
she had best not know.”

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.990
those being the Hanseatic trade secrets.

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:54.110
But despite this, in practice, it was all
very much tolerated by the entire league.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:58.170
There’s even a law found in one of the books
at the London Kontor, which states that if

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:02.950
two or more merchants were planning to bring
women to the confines of the Yard, they had

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:07.769
to decide prior to entering the kontor which
woman shall lay with whom as to not repeat

00:10:07.769 --> 00:10:10.100
an incident that occurred previously.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:15.110
Which presumably was a fight between two guys
over a girl.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:19.870
Back in Bergen another 3 years have passed
and you have been promoted to the title of

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:24.170
Gesell, which in english would be something
like journeyman or junior partner.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:28.740
This basically means you work directly under
one of the Masters also known as just a Merchant

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:29.740
in the Kontor.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:33.510
You go with him on sailing expeditions, to
business meetings, and sometimes you’re

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:36.000
even allowed to make your own small business
decisions.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:40.190
You gather valuable knowledge about how the
Hanseatic league operates, what are its rules

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:41.220
etc.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:45.120
After a couple of years of this and almost
at the end of your 7 to 10 year stay at the

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.500
Bergen Kontor you’re finally promoted to
the status of a Meister.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.430
Basically meaning master in German.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.930
This means you’re finally allowed to make
your own way in life and the League.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:59.350
You no longer have to work under any merchant,
you can conduct your own business within the

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:04.089
league, make your own trade deals, and even
participate in the Kontor and the League elections.

00:11:04.089 --> 00:11:08.800
You can also run for offices if you want,
like Hausmeister, the head of a Yard, the

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:13.870
Achtzehner, one of the 18 councillors of a
Kontor, or Olderleute, one of the three elderman

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:14.870
in the kontor.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:19.820
If you are very ambitious you can even become
a representative of a Hanseatic city on the

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:24.959
Hansetag, the highest Hanseatic Office which
meets in Lubeck and basically has the final

00:11:24.959 --> 00:11:27.120
say in every Hanseatic affair.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:31.580
But hold all those thoughts, because you’re
technically not done yet.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:38.110
Going from a Gesell to a Meister you have
go through not one, not two, but three initiation

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:42.519
ceremonies, which in Bryggen, are known as
the Hanseatic games.

00:11:42.519 --> 00:11:43.519
So let's begin.

00:11:43.519 --> 00:11:47.029
“The Smoke Test”
The first initiation ceremony is a spectacle

00:11:47.029 --> 00:11:48.230
for the entire city.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:51.079
Crowdes from all over Bergen gather to witness
your hazing.

00:11:51.079 --> 00:11:56.860
“(Cough) ok I can’t do that voice for
the entire time sorry”.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:00.220
So the first initiation ceremony is a spectacle
for the entire city.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:03.139
Crowdes from all over Bergen gather to witness
your hazing.

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:09.399
The boats in the Harbor are decorated in colorful
flags, ornaments, etc. also each Yard is proudly

00:12:09.399 --> 00:12:11.990
waving its own special flag as well.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:16.769
Senior members of the Kontor pass in a procession
through the city, followed by the Stubenjungens

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:17.769
with buckets.

00:12:17.769 --> 00:12:21.790
The Stubenjungens gathered into the buckets
all the filthiest things they can find on

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:26.050
the streets as the procession goes along,
sometimes even being helped by the locals

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:28.610
who brought their own dirty things to put
in the bucket.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:33.649
The parade is also accompanied by a jester,
masked figures, and two people entertaining

00:12:33.649 --> 00:12:36.790
the crowd, dressed as the poorest peasants
imaginable.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:40.089
Ou and you along with other initiates are
there as well.

00:12:40.089 --> 00:12:43.959
Once the procession enters the guild hall
of the Bryggen you are tied and hauled up

00:12:43.959 --> 00:12:45.279
into the chimney.

00:12:45.279 --> 00:12:49.820
After that the Stubenjungens drop all the
contents of their buckets into the fireplace

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:51.380
and a fire is started.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:55.639
During this time you are repeatedly lowered
from the chimney and questioned on various

00:12:55.639 --> 00:12:56.970
merchant knowledge.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:00.930
When the Senior Merchants see you are at the
bring of suffocation you are promptly taken

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:04.990
out of the chimney and dosed with 6 buckets
of ice cold water.

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:08.040
Congratulations you have passed the first
task.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:11.810
“The Water Test”
There is a giant banquet held to your and

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:13.320
other initiates honor.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.709
There is plenty of drinking, eating, singing,
etc.

00:13:16.709 --> 00:13:20.301
However when this stops, you’re promptly
stripped off from all of your clothing, this

00:13:20.301 --> 00:13:24.850
is so that everyone can make sure you’re
a male because allegedly one time a woman

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:28.110
was almost admitted to the league (ha the
horror).

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:32.151
Once completely naked you’re taken out on
a boat in to the harbor where you’re thrown

00:13:32.151 --> 00:13:33.850
into the ice cold water.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:38.090
Everytime you try to get back up into the
boat you’re beaten back into the water with

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:39.090
a stick.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:43.089
Keep in mind while all of this is happening
everyone is quite drunk.

00:13:43.089 --> 00:13:46.870
This continues on for a couple of minutes
until you’re brought back up into the boat

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:48.449
and back to the Kontor.

00:13:48.449 --> 00:13:51.490
Congratulations you have passed the second
task.

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:55.260
“The Flogging Test”
Happening on a separate day than the actual

00:13:55.260 --> 00:14:00.240
flogging, you and other initiates are required
to go on a procession through the town to

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:05.040
the St Mary’s church cemetery where the
locals have already gathered in large numbers.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:09.860
You and other initiates then take turns and
climb on a tree, from which you yell out in

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:16.149
minute details, every sexual act you had with
every woman whilst at Bergen, apparently the

00:14:16.149 --> 00:14:18.520
locals found this very amusing.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:22.699
On the day of the last initiation, another
procession of the most senior members of the

00:14:22.699 --> 00:14:26.920
Kontor, and drummers, go through the town
in the morning to the nearby forest where

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:30.190
they cut the most painfully looking branches
from a tree.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:33.990
Then they come back to the Kontor where they
give an address to all the initiates about

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:38.350
the importance of the league, it’s community
and that you can still back out if you don’t

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.660
want to be a member.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:44.800
After that another giant banquete is held
at noon with music, singing, drinking, etc.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:49.530
Apparently special care is taken at this time
that all the initiates are very intoxicated

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.300
by the time of the flogging.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:55.320
Than the branches that have been cut earlier
in the day are given to the most muscular

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:59.860
member of the Kontor and the initiates are
wiped by them until it’s deemed by the senior

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:02.149
members of the Kontor “that’s enough”.

00:15:02.149 --> 00:15:06.839
After this the initiates are given even more
alcohol during which if they pass out, they’re

00:15:06.839 --> 00:15:08.139
thrown into the local well.

00:15:08.139 --> 00:15:12.720
If you survived, congratulations, you have
passed the third and last task.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:16.779
You’re now officially a full fledged merchant
of the hanseatic League.

00:15:16.779 --> 00:15:21.779
I would also like to point out that even though
very uncommon some members did died during

00:15:21.779 --> 00:15:23.699
these initiation ceremonies.

00:15:23.699 --> 00:15:25.150
But you don’t have to worry about that.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:29.610
You survived and you can now either stay in
the Kontor and run for an office there, return

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:34.190
back to Rostock and conduct trade there, or
go anywhere else to conduct business within

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:35.329
the Hanseatic league.

00:15:35.329 --> 00:15:38.791
You can now also finally marry someone and
maybe you found a girl you fancy while you

00:15:38.791 --> 00:15:40.850
were in Bergen, so you’ll decide to stay.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:44.170
Who knows the choice is yours.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:48.670
Now before this video ends I want to emphasize
this was just one representation of a life

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:51.480
that a Hanseatic merchant might have had.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:56.450
The Hanseatic League was a giant medieval
trade guild spanning multiple centuries.

00:15:56.450 --> 00:16:01.350
The life experiences of a Hansa merchant in
the 13th century differed widely from a Hansa

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.089
merchant in the 16th century.

00:16:03.089 --> 00:16:07.050
In the later half of the leagues existence,
there where even instances of German speaking

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:10.449
Slavic and Baltic people becoming merchants
within the guild.

00:16:10.449 --> 00:16:14.389
Plus even in this small snippet of time in
the early 15th century that I have shown in

00:16:14.389 --> 00:16:19.910
this video, the experiences of each merchant
in the Hansa where very different as well.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:25.510
For example the Bergen kontor was notorious
even within the Hansa for it’s hazing, closed

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:28.320
off community, and unique administrative structure.

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:32.250
The London Kontor on the other hand was a
much more open ended community without such

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:33.930
rigidly defined social structures.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.339
They were still there, just not as harsh.

00:16:36.339 --> 00:16:41.040
In the Novgorod kontor young merchants where
even encouraged to live amongst Russian farmers

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.959
so they learned the language, because that
would be beneficial for their trade later

00:16:44.959 --> 00:16:45.959
on.

00:16:45.959 --> 00:16:49.540
And many merchants who signed up with the
Hanseatic league didn’t even live in a Kontor,

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:54.200
they simply worked within a well known medieval
apprenticeship structure under a merchant

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:58.450
“master”, going from one Hansa city to
another Hansa city and conducting in layman's

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.450
terms, trade.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:04.030
They did this until they reached a stage to
be elevated to a Master within the Hansa themselves,

00:17:04.030 --> 00:17:08.500
after which just like you becoming a Master
in the Kontor they could conduct trade on

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.380
their own anywhere in the Hanseatic League.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:16.010
There are so many variables within the Hanseatic
League that changed depending on many other

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:20.959
variables that the only way I saw it possible
to present how the Hanseatic League operated

00:17:20.959 --> 00:17:26.780
was through showing just one specific time
period in one specific geographical area.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:31.740
Otherwise this video would have had too many
asterisks attached to everything I said.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:35.539
Hope you enjoyed the video, don’t forget
I have Patreon you can support me on and there’s

00:17:35.539 --> 00:17:39.130
more information, clarifications and corrections
in the description as always.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:41.629
My name is M. Laser and stick around for History.

